161-Structure
162-
163:Work events within Senseye are composed of the following required
164-attributes:
165-
166:- Timestamp: the date, time and time zone that the work took place
167:- Message: A free text description of the work undertaken
168:- Asset ID: Either the Senseye or External ID of the asset the work was
169-  performed on
170:- Is Routine: Whether the event was routine or non-routine
171:- Work Activity: The type of work undertaken
172-
173-In addition to these required attributes, the following optional
174-attribute can be provided:
175-
176:- Failure Mode: Identifies the failure encountered on the asset
177-
178-Each will be described in more detail in the following sections.
179-
180:Timestamp¶
181-
182:The eventTime attribute should identify when the work was completed.
183-This allows Senseye to learn how the failure evolved to the point of
184-intervention and implies that any changes in data may be related to the
185:recent work on the asset.
186-
187:Ideally the date and time provided should be as close to the work being
188:completed as possible. If an accurate timestamp is not available, the
189:application prefers timestamps which are known to be after the work
190-being completed, rather than before.
191-
192:The timestamp should include date, time and time zone, see the timestamp
193-documentation for more information on the required format.
194-
195-Message¶
196-
197:The message is a free text description which explains the work. It is
198-shown within the application and often used as contextual information
199-when exploring cases and root causes.
200-
201-Asset ID¶
202-
203:The asset which the work was performed on can be identified by either
204-its Senseye ID or an External ID. Typically the External ID used in this
205-case would be the ID of the asset within your maintenance system - you
206-can read more about configuring and using External IDs here.
207-
208:Is Routine¶
209-
210:This boolean attribute identifies whether the work was planned or not.
211-It is used in reporting to allow insight to be gained from your
212-maintenance records.
213-
214:Work Activity¶
215-
216:Work activity explains what work was undertaken. The values are codified
217-within Senseye, they rarely change and are common across all assets. The
218-current list is:
